\title{The Real Line and an Open Interval Are Homeomorphic}
\taxon{Example}
\p{
    The map
    ##{
        f:\mathbb{R}\longrightarrow(0,1),
        \qquad
        f(x)=\frac12+\frac{1}{\pi}\arctan x
    }
    is a bijection. It is continuous, and its inverse
    ##{
        f^{-1}(t)=\tan\left(\pi\left(t-\frac12\right)\right)
    }
    is continuous on #{(0,1)}. Hence #{f} is a [homeomorphism](def-005O).
    Topologically, boundedness and total length do not distinguish the open
    interval from the whole real line.
}
